  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiru II Fadama Farmers&apos; Cooperative Sorghum EEI</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kiru II Fadama Farmers Cooperative Society (KFFCS) is an organization wholly owned by a group of small-scale low-income farmers located in and around Kiru town in Kiru Local Government Area of Kano State in Nigeria. The Cooperatives members produce Sorghum for direct consumption and for marketing. Growth in the food, beverage and animal feed industries has led to increased demand for high quality Sorghum.</narrative>
  </description>
